  "structure": {
    "block_count": 50,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "15 Oh-So-Charming British Baby Girl Names",
        "text_sha256": "8006048c15b395b47f14aed54fddfdf4dc261b189d3aa768a6d5c01f691e9b3c",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Updates to copy, sources, and formatting.",
        "text_sha256": "2bf448333081ffc8549a45a6c4b7fc711ee4b93575f0fffd3c4a6212c13581c2",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "british baby girl names",
        "text_sha256": "bd54cc565a5d7a873897b16cd867c22788492de20dba2770cf32ef5ade7e4f4d",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Bryce, Greer, and more cheerful baby girl names from England, Scotland, and Wales.",
        "text_sha256": "8eadea7ea4106683226429e0783bcd3e9bb664f094c986e8a2d0a576da04052e",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If you're looking for a joyful-sounding baby girl name to celebrate your daughter-to-be, there might be one (or several!) on this list of British baby names for girls that you'll love.",
        "text_sha256": "4802fee4cc110151d61bcdf83cad66087c56aca92efc63643edc79e9c24f4038",
        "word_count": 31
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Hailing from England, Scotland, and Wales, these British names have more than sparkle and vivaciousness in common; like many British boy names , most of these names for girls can be shortened into cool nicknames that are equal parts fun and cheerful.",
        "text_sha256": "eaf1bf8ccabb700137d9d74fa3430c78e9f676ece56415485d62216939887ed6",
        "word_count": 42
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Want more charming monikers from across the pond? We've got endless baby name inspiration in the What to Expect app .",
        "text_sha256": "aba5cfbd3de22053d5daf2fde57cdc9f4ada218c53ea30b5286b33506d313966",
        "word_count": 21
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Adeline . This English name could be pronounced two different ways — \"Adelynn\" or \"Adeleen\" — depending on your preference. It's a form of the German name Adelaide, which means \"noble and serene.\"",
        "text_sha256": "5dc19f6b494fe8e6abeb1a5236b870f67260bdcb704a49545c375402e9d281da",
        "word_count": 33
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Bryce. This Welsh name could be used for a girl (think actress Bryce Dallas Howard) or a boy. It means \"alert, ambitious.\"",
        "text_sha256": "3b95f8701739dc5aa577ef30d569e95c739d731f568f54442ee91da93c6cb4f3",
        "word_count": 22
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Dylan. Here's another gender-neutral name that's rising in popularity for girls and boys. It means \"born of the sea\" in the Welsh tradition.",
        "text_sha256": "6e33d07bfc69a1ddea4cddd9b7512779b509055b73233a91139d9d619db0e3dc",
        "word_count": 23
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Ebrill. This beautiful Welsh name means \"born in April.\" Due in April? Ebrill would be more than appropriate.",
        "text_sha256": "87ccfd05cbc87a55730a6da0da3248744fce4d5a5d6ad4b350e354405ecf0a80",
        "word_count": 18
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Edie. Looking for something short and sweet? This familiar form of Edith — which means \"rich gift\" — may suit your baby girl perfectly.",
        "text_sha256": "2910571f5d7e6c1e642f360ad9acbadd697ebb5ea0f0bc8bfc611bddc023b104",
        "word_count": 24
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Georgina. If you want a name that lends itself to cute nicknames, this English pick might be the one for you. It's a familiar form of Georgia, which means \"farmer\" in the Greek tradition. You could call her Gigi or Georgie for short.",
        "text_sha256": "dd0a6ea1c395b8f93d69bd6aaaf1c31440fdb8b42e6ac5c9f50a1d82719d2c0f",
        "word_count": 43
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Greer. This Scottish name is unique but still easy to pronounce. It would pair particularly well with a long last name. It means \"vigilant.\"",
        "text_sha256": "60f95f2eca263c97c5b3181b45929dbeffbf33ebc168196f4ee1dc1ff8254009",
        "word_count": 24
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Henrietta. This is a strong, vintage-sounding name, which means \"ruler of the household\" in the English tradition. Etta would be a really sweet nickname.",
        "text_sha256": "c90e179b48229b6d49436cd3e9c0d2de5f2697865e233f3906ffa907db29e955",
        "word_count": 24
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Joleen. How about a feminine name and a gender-neutral nickname? Joleen/Jo is the best of both worlds. It's a familiar form of Jolene, which means \"God will increase\" in the Hebrew tradition.",
        "text_sha256": "c9c2e4eff29250617dc8f3d7a81464879d03728920eaa9042ee4967f72ca2d51",
        "word_count": 32
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Lynlee. This stunning English name actually sounds like two first names. It's a form of Lynn, which means \"waterfall.\"",
        "text_sha256": "b91ca7b24c21cd4690a9090d7e71046a7e2054362469ff5437d79ea1c9cd4126",
        "word_count": 19
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Marjorie. We love this old-fashioned name that's coming back in fashion. It's a Scottish version of Mary (Hebrew for \"bitter\"). You could call her Marjie for short.",
        "text_sha256": "d9173e1941946a43cf3f0119cb23f6ed0a6ea5bf245edc74d15c5098a7c46de6",
        "word_count": 27
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Marlena. Yet another name that sounds like a combination of two… this one's an English version of Marlene, meaning \"high tower\" in the Greek tradition.",
        "text_sha256": "1729f8fedb4636b14663f7569dcd69efe58724bf33c5f424d0aa6dcd9efc9eb9",
        "word_count": 25
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Rosie. Considering Rose but want something just a bit more familiar and endearing? This English version could work.",
        "text_sha256": "1b3ae6832a18ceb59a37335d8799a961766439827d175cbfd2cfaa9be4c1d15a",
        "word_count": 18
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Starling. This English name — meaning, no real surprise here, \"bird\" — is ideal if you love the outdoors and want to cultivate an appreciation of nature in your little one. Plus, it's simply gorgeous, even shortened to Star.",
        "text_sha256": "4fb98b30b434fc5666eee9190515bdb67abfaf0f63ca19c05a39bcebb06625bb",
        "word_count": 39
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Teagan. This Welsh name means \"beautiful, attractive\" and like many of the other British names above, it could be used for a girl or a boy.",
        "text_sha256": "f0b958b9b005a2fd6d0b38feedfc5d77f40c047a717ca32efa603ac5c7ad9714",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
